      "url": "https://www.rentex.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/CL5-Data-Sheet.pdf",
      "note": "Yamaha CL5 technical data sheet (dealer-hosted copy of the manufacturer sheet), opened 2026-11-12: 1053 (W) x 299 (H) x 667 (D) mm, 36 kg, 34 motorised 100 mm faders, AC inlet V-lock type (the IEC letter is not named: iec-c14 assumed, plan assumedConnectors power-in). The CL owner manual (data.yamaha.com), opened the same day, documents the panels: rear OMNI IN 1-8 (XLR-3-31 female, +48 V per input), OMNI OUT 1-8 (XLR-3-32 male), DIGITAL OUT AES/EBU (XLR male), Dante PRIMARY and SECONDARY on etherCON, NETWORK (RJ45, CL Editor and StageMix), word clock in and out (BNC), MIDI, GPI (D-sub), lamp XLR4 x3, three mini-YGDAI slots, a power switch beside AC IN; front talkback (XLR female) and stereo phones; USB on the top panel. Not modelled: MIDI, GPI, lamp, slots, USB, the redundant DC input. 8 of 8 omni inputs and outputs are modelled (the unit has more only through slots and Dante). Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, faders, knobs and screens drawn without lettering, no photo, no logo. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess) and the side profile is an estimate drawn from the three outer sizes (no drawing opened). Connector genders not stated by the source follow the convention input = female, output = male."
    }
  ]
